(Description)
Given two sorted arrays nums1 and nums2 of size m and n respectively, return the median of the two sorted arrays.
The overall run time complexity should be O(log (m+n)).

--- Solution ---
class Solution {
    public double findMedianSortedArrays(int[] nums1, int[] nums2) {
        if (nums1.length > nums2.length) {
            return findMedianSortedArrays(nums2, nums1);
        }
        
        int m = nums1.length;
        int n = nums2.length;

        int left = 0;
        int right = m;

        int half = (m + n + 1) / 2;

        while (left <= right) {
            int part1 = (left + right) / 2;
            int part2 = half - part1;

            int left1 = (part1 == 0) ? Integer.MIN_VALUE : nums1[part1 - 1];
            int right1 = (part1 == m) ? Integer.MAX_VALUE : nums1[part1];
            int left2 = (part2 == 0) ? Integer.MIN_VALUE : nums2[part2 - 1];
            int right2 = (part2 == n) ? Integer.MAX_VALUE : nums2[part2];

            if (left1 <= right2 && left2 <= right1) {
                if ((m+n) % 2 == 1) {
                    return Math.max(left1, left2);
                }

                int maxLeft = Math.max(left1, left2);
                int minRight = Math.min(right1, right2);

                return (maxLeft + minRight) / 2.0;
            }
            else if (left1 > right2) {
                right = part1 - 1;
            }
            else {
                left = part1 + 1;
            }
        }

        return 0.0;
    }
}

--- Approach ---
Even though the concept of this problem is easy, the time complexity made it difficult to solve.
Because of the time complexity, the two given arrays counldn't be merged or searching with loop statements.

Therefore, binary search for two arrays is the key point of the algorithm.
Because the two arrays were sorted, if first median is smaller than second median, it could be figured out that left part of first median is smaller than left part of the second median.
Then, each medains could generate two numbers, left(represents left part of the median) & right(represents right part).

In the algorithm, Binary search find the exact point that first left is smaller or equal than second right and second left is smaller than first right.
And that point is the median of two arrays exactly.
Else if it was not median, it moves its pointers follwed by the result of comparison of each left and right values.
